   "reasoning_summary": "C12H20O8 has DoU 3. The 13C data show a beta-glucopyranosyl unit (101.1, 75.9, 75.6, 72.9, 69.6, 60.7) and a six-carbon aglycone. That aglycone comprises an ester C=O (174.5), two CH-O carbons (74.9, 70.7), two CH2 (34.9, 34.6) and CH3 (20.4). The remaining two unsaturations are the lactone C=O and the lactone ring. This matches parasorboside, the 4-O-glucoside of 4-hydroxy-6-methyl-delta-valerolactone. The 1H data agree: CH2 alpha to C=O at 2.80/2.74, ring CH2 at 2.19/1.83, CH3 at 1.34, H-4 at 4.41 and anomeric H at 4.51. Lactone H-6 is assumed to lie under the HOD signal at 4.85. The 15 listed C-H protons plus that hidden H-6 give 16, and the 4 OH protons are exchanged, accounting for all 20 H."
  },
